<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Paladin Guild</h1>
<p>The holy order of the paladins keeps its guild hall in Midgaard, by the 
Cathedral square: a monastery with its yard, barracks, armoury, stables, 
the Shrine to Gehron and a holy meditation chamber. Its head is Reignier, 
the Guild Master.
</p><p>To join, stand before Reignier and type <a cmd='#'>join</a>. The order accepts only 
the devoted and pure of heart: conjurers, sorcerers, dark knights, 
assassins, thieves and necromancers are turned away. First you must 
prove yourself worthy by finishing the Paladin's Guild quest; Reignier 
sends you to Joan the Pure to begin it.
</p><p>A paladin must stay good. The order's trainers won't teach anyone whose 
alignment has fallen below good (+350), and a truly evil soul who walks 
into the holy halls is drained and thrown out into the street. To leave 
the guild, insult the Master; but a member who is banished can never come 
back.
</p><p><br />
